---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalDoc from '~/components/widgets/LegalDoc.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '~/config/contact';
import { site, siteHost } from '~/config/site';

const host = siteHost();
const legalName = CONTACT.businessName;
const dbaName = site.name;
const entityLabel =
  legalName === dbaName ? legalName : `${legalName} (doing business as ${dbaName})`;

const analyticsProviders = [
  site.analytics.googleTagManagerId.trim() && 'Google Tag Manager',
  site.analytics.googleAnalyticsId.trim() && 'Google Analytics',
].filter(Boolean);
const analyticsProviderSentence = analyticsProviders.length
  ? `The analytics tools currently in use are ${analyticsProviders.join(' and ')}.`
  : 'No third-party analytics tools are currently configured.';

const metadata = {
  title: `Privacy Policy | ${dbaName}`,
  description: `How ${dbaName} collects, uses, and protects information from the website, forms, chapters, and the self-assessment.`,
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};

const headingClass = 'text-h4 font-heading font-normal text-heading mb-4';
const bodyClass = 'text-body-lg font-normal leading-[160%] text-muted';
const listClass = `${bodyClass} mt-4 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5`;
const linkClass = 'btn-link';
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Fragment slot="header" />
  <LegalDoc title="Privacy Policy">
      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>1. Who we are and what this policy covers</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          This Privacy Policy explains how {entityLabel}, referred to here as "we," "us," or "our," collects, uses, and
          shares information through {host}, our forms and communications, and our chapters and activities.
        </p>
        <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
          This policy does not cover Athena Clinic, Lulu, or any other third-party service we link to. Those
          organizations have their own privacy practices. Athena Clinic is a medical practice, and information you give
          Athena Clinic is handled under its own privacy notices, not this policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>2. The self-assessment</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          The self-assessment runs entirely in your web browser. Your answers and your results are not sent to us,
          stored by us, or shared with Athena Clinic, our analytics providers, or anyone else. Although Athena Clinic
          sponsors the self-assessment, Athena Clinic does not receive your answers or results through this website.
        </p>
        <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
          We may record that the self-assessment pages were visited, in the same way we record visits to other pages,
          but we do not record the answers you enter or the result you receive. Your answers are cleared when you close
          or reload the page. If you print or save your results, that copy is yours to keep. If you later choose to
          share your results with a chapter, a physician, or Athena Clinic, that information is handled by whoever you
          give it to.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>3. Information we collect</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          <strong class="font-medium text-heading">Information you give us.</strong> When you book a first visit, join a
          waitlist, apply to start a chapter, contact a chapter, or send us an inquiry, we collect the details you
          provide, such as your name, email address, phone number, the chapter or session you are interested in, and
          anything you choose to include in a message.
        </p>
        <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
          <strong class="font-medium text-heading">Information collected at activities.</strong> When you attend a
          session, a chapter may collect sign-in details, signed participation agreements, and emergency contact
          information. Sessions may also be photographed or recorded.
        </p>
        <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
          <strong class="font-medium text-heading">Information collected automatically.</strong> When you visit the
          website, we and our service providers may automatically collect limited technical information, such as your IP
          address, browser and device type, the pages you visit, the date and time of your visit, and the site that
          referred you.
        </p>
        <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
          <strong class="font-medium text-heading">Payment information.</strong> If we collect dues or sell products
          directly, payments are handled by a third-party payment processor. We do not receive or store your full card
          number.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>4. Health information</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          We do not ask you to provide health information through this website. Some people choose to tell us about an
          injury, condition, or limitation, for example in a message field, so that a session can be adapted for them.
          If you do, we use that information only to arrange your participation, share it only with the chapter lead or
          session leader who needs it, and do not use it for marketing. Please do not send detailed medical information
          or medical records through the website or by email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>5. How we use information</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>We use the information we collect to:</p>
        <ul class={listClass}>
          <li>Respond to your inquiries and arrange your first visit</li>
          <li>Connect you with the right chapter and keep you informed about sessions you asked about</li>
          <li>Run chapters and activities, including safety and emergency arrangements</li>
          <li>Review chapter applications</li>
          <li>Send updates or newsletters you have signed up for</li>
          <li>Understand how the website is used and improve it</li>
          <li>Protect the security of the website and prevent misuse</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>6. How we share information</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>We share information only as described here:</p>
        <ul class={listClass}>
          <li>
            With chapter leads and volunteers, who receive the details you submit about their chapter so they can
            respond to you and arrange your visit. They may use only that information for {dbaName} purposes
          </li>
          <li>
            With service providers that help us operate the website and our communications, such as hosting, form
            handling, email, text messaging, and analytics providers, who may use the information only to provide
            services to us
          </li>
          <li>With Athena Clinic, only if you ask us to share your information with them</li>
          <li>
            When required by law, or when we believe in good faith that disclosure is needed to protect the safety,
            rights, or property of any person
          </li>
          <li>
            In connection with a reorganization, merger, or transfer of {dbaName}, subject to this policy
          </li>
          <li>With your consent</li>
        </ul>
        <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
          We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for targeted advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          The website may use cookies and similar technologies that are needed for the site to work, and analytics tools
          that tell us how the site is used in aggregate, such as which pages are visited. {analyticsProviderSentence}{' '}
          We do not use analytics tools to capture what you type into the self-assessment. You can control or delete
          cookies through your browser settings. Where required by law, we honor browser signals such as Global Privacy
          Control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>8. Emails and text messages</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          You can unsubscribe from our emails using the link in any message. You can stop text messages by replying
          STOP. We may still contact you about a request you have made, such as a visit you booked.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>9. Photographs and recordings</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          Photographs and recordings from sessions may be published on the website, in podcasts, and in other {dbaName}{' '}
          materials. If you do not want to appear, tell the session leader before the session begins. If you appear in
          published material and would like it removed, contact us and we will make reasonable efforts to do so.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>10. How long we keep information</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          We keep personal information only as long as we need it for the purposes described in this policy, including
          to respond to you, run chapters and activities, and meet legal, insurance, and record-keeping obligations.
          Signed participation agreements may be kept for longer periods where needed for legal or insurance reasons.
          When information is no longer needed, we delete it or de-identify it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>11. Security</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical measures to protect the information we hold. No
          website, email, or storage system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee the security of information
          you send us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>12. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you, or to stop contacting
          you, by emailing
          <a class={linkClass} href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. Depending on where you live, you
          may have additional rights under state law, such as the right to know how your information is used or to
          appeal a decision about your request. We will verify your identity before acting on a request and will not
          treat you differently for making one.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>13. Children</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          This website and our activities are intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
          children under 13. If you believe a child has given us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>14. Links to other websites</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          This website links to other websites, including Athena Clinic, Lulu, and podcast and map services. We are not
          responsible for their privacy practices, and we encourage you to read their privacy policies before sharing
          information with them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>15. Where information is processed</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          We are based in the United States, and information we collect is stored and processed in the United States.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>16. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          We may update this policy from time to time. The current version is always posted on this page with its
          effective date. If we make a significant change to how we handle personal information, we will make that clear
          on this page or contact you directly where required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class={headingClass}>17. Contact</h2>
        <p class={bodyClass}>
          Questions or requests about this policy can be sent to:<br /><br />
          {legalName}<br />
          {CONTACT.address.street && (
            <>
              {CONTACT.address.street}
              <br />
            </>
          )}
          {CONTACT.address.cityLine}<br />
          Email: <a class={linkClass} href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a><br />
          Phone: <a class={linkClass} href={CONTACT.phone.href}>{CONTACT.phone.display}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
  </LegalDoc>
</Layout>
